   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "close() and the with clause"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "After use, file_object.close() frees the memory given to the file and writes any unsaved data to it. If the file object is reassigned to another file, Python closes the earlier one automatically. The with clause, with open(name, mode) as f:, closes the file automatically when the block ends, even if an exception occurs, so it is the preferred style."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "file_object.close()"
    },
    {
     "en": "with open(\"myfile.txt\", \"r+\") as myObject:"
    },
    {
     "en": "No explicit close() needed inside with"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "After use, file_object.close() frees the memory given to the file and writes any unsaved data to it. If the file object is reassigned to another file, Python closes the earlier one automatically. The with clause, with open(name, mode) as f:, closes the file automatically when the block ends, even if an exception occurs, so it is the preferred style.",
    "kn": "ಬಳಕೆಯ ನಂತರ close() ಕಡತ ಮುಚ್ಚುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಉಳಿದ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಬರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. with ಉಪವಾಕ್ಯ ಬ್ಲಾಕ್ ಮುಗಿದಾಗ ಕಡತವನ್ನು ಸ್ವಯಂಚಾಲಿತವಾಗಿ ಮುಚ್ಚುತ್ತದೆ, ದೋಷ ಬಂದರೂ ಸಹ."
   }
